## Plan: Invites UI + Send + Resend

Fix the missing invites-page action by implementing a visible resend-email control, then add backend email delivery so invites are sent on create and can be resent for active codes. Use SMTP-first configuration for fastest MVP, reuse the same active code for resend, include a direct register link with prefilled code, and enforce resend throttling (3 per code per hour).

**Steps**
1. Stabilize the invites page baseline and remove the current component resolution blocker in the Angular invites feature so the page compiles reliably. This step blocks all other frontend invite work.
2. Add explicit resend action UX to the invites grid in the admin invites page (button state, success/error feedback, loading state, disabled rules for used/expired/no-email rows). Depends on step 1.
3. Extend frontend invite API service with resend endpoint call and typed response handling; wire component methods and optimistic refresh behavior. Depends on step 1; parallel with step 4.
4. Introduce backend email infrastructure with SMTP settings, a single invite-email service, and a consistent invite email template payload (org name, invite code, expiry, register URL). Parallel with step 3.
5. Update create-invite endpoint to send email when an invitee email is provided (send-on-create path), while still supporting code-only creation when email is blank. Depends on step 4.
6. Add resend endpoint for existing code: POST organization/{orgId}/registration-codes/{codeId}/resend. Enforce tenant access, block used/expired/no-email codes, and apply throttle max 3 per code per hour. Depends on step 4.
7. Add resend audit trail fields/events so resend attempts are visible and enforceable. Depends on step 6.
8. Add registration URL composition for email link (register page with org + code query params) and verify frontend register screen can consume prefilled code without regressions. Depends on steps 4 and 6.
9. Run end-to-end verification for: create invite + auto email, resend active code, throttle behavior, invalid resend paths, and role/tenant access checks. Depends on steps 1-8.
10. Update tracking docs with outcomes and any remaining follow-up: MASTER_TODO_LIST.md and NOTES_DEFECTS_USER_TODO. Depends on step 9.

